  "dct_description_sm": [
    "<p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:1.5rem; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><span style='font-family:Arial, &quot;sans-serif&quot;;'><a href='https://gis.conservationhalton.net/doc/opendatahub/Metadata/CH_Metadata_WatershedReportCard2018_Subwatershed.pdf' style='color:rgb(0, 94, 149); font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Click Here</a> for Metadata. The polygon feature class represents the letter grades associated with Forest Condition and Surface Water Quality resource indicators at the watershed and subwatershed level. Grades for surface water quality are based on chemical (phosphorus concentrations) and biological (benthic invertebrates) indicators of water quality across the watershed. Grades for forest conditions are based on the percentage of forest cover, forest interior (100m from the forest edge) and streamside vegetation that is forested. Streamside forests in particular help improve water quality.</span></p><p style='margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:1.5rem; font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><span style='font-family:Arial, sans-serif;'>The grading scale is as follows, A - Excellent; B - Good; C - Fair; D - Poor; and F - Very Poor.</span></p>"
